{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kellner","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Five fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E, and B→F♯ — are each narrowed by ⅕ of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Pythagorean comma, equal to ⁵√(2¹⁴\/3⁷) ≈ 697.654 cents. The remaining seven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Proposed by Kellner as a reconstruction of Bach’s own tuning, published in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Das Musikinstrument"}]},{"text":" 26 (1977). The choice of five fifths and their positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mirrors the structure of Werckmeister III while spreading the tempering more evenly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/kellner","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kellner"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Kellner (Herbert Anton Kellner, 1977).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Type Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kellner"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"title":"kellner","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE7kellnerAEvpZ"},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that describes a musical tuning system."}],"title":"TuningSystem"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem/kellner":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/kellner","title":"kellner","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kellner (Herbert Anton Kellner, 1977)."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"kellner"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"WellTemperament","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kellner"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths."}],"title":"WellTemperament"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","title":"IvorTuning","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"}}}